## Managing the interface

Terraform can manage the initial interface created by Contentful on first
activation without import.

When changing a Content Type and its Editor Interface together, use the same
provider configuration and reference the Content Type resource. This lets the
provider account for its own activations during the apply. Separate provider
aliases do not share that coordination. If another edit causes a version
conflict, review a refreshed plan before applying again.

After removing Terraform management, import the existing interface to manage it
again. Deleting its parent Content Type or environment can still delete the
interface.

